<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarosius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarosius was a ruler of the Alans in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-caucasus">North Caucasus</a> in the mid-sixth century, known from the Byzantine historian Menander Protector. A friend of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, he helped the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avar</a> envoys reach the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-i">Justinian I</a> around 558, and he later received the Byzantine envoy Zemarchus returning from the Western Turks. His control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> passes made him valuable to Byzantium in its wars with Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>.</p></div>
